## Product rules

- Tags are **global**. Library sources and Rooms are **per project**. Default project name: **Palace**.
- The same disk folder cannot belong to two projects (`SourceFolder.Path` is UNIQUE).
- Delete = Recycle Bin + catalog row (`DeleteAssetsAsync`). Multi-delete must stay interactive: `BeginBusy` before awaits, suppress watcher notifications (`WatcherService.SuppressNotifications` + short linger), batch catalog delete, then prune mosaic / `_allAssets` in place (`MosaicDelete`) — do **not** call `RefreshQuietAsync` or `ScanService.ScanSourceAsync` after Library delete. Watcher parent-folder `Changed` (LastWrite) must not full-scan the source; only directory Created/Renamed indexes that subtree (`ScanDirectoryAsync`). Coalesce watcher UI refresh; ignore no-op events. Do not hydrate/Open online-only files to delete — `StorageFile.DeleteAsync` recycles placeholders.
- **Move / folder ops go through `FileOpService`** (never `File.Move` in a ViewModel or code-behind). Every source and destination path must resolve to a **local** watched source of the current project (`FileOpService.ResolveRoot`); anything else is refused. Writes also go through `ResolveWritableRoot`: the deepest watched source across **all** projects must belong to this project (no writing into another project's nested root), and no folder below the source may be a junction / symlink (`LinkedFolderBetween`, `DirectoryInfo.LinkTarget`; cloud placeholders are not links). A folder that contains another watched source is never renamed. Rename keeps `IsOrphan` and moves the folder back if the catalog rebase fails. A move cancelled after files already moved stops and still journals them for Undo. File ops run one at a time per project (a static per-project gate also covering Undo's read / run / mark). A failed journal write reverts the operation with its Undo steps; a move whose catalog write and move-back both fail stops the batch and says to rescan. Never overwrite: clashes get `name (2).ext` (also when a stale catalog row owns the name), `File.Move(overwrite: false)`. Never read originals; online-only placeholders move only inside their own watched source (a rename that stays a placeholder) and are skipped otherwise. Folder delete is **empty folders only** (hidden files count) and source roots can't be renamed or deleted. Each operation logs one `FileOpBatch` so **Undo** (`BtnUndo`, Ctrl+Z on the page `PreviewKeyDown` so text boxes keep their own undo, `InfUndo` toast's `BtnUndoToast`) reverses the newest batch of the project: files go back (unique name if the old spot is taken) and catalog rows are restored. Move follows the delete rules: `BeginBusy`, watcher suppressed by the service, mosaic updated in place (`MosaicMove`: prune when tiles leave the viewed folder, re-query when they move into a subfolder of it, rewrite paths in flat views) — no `RefreshQuietAsync` / source scan. Move acts on the selected tiles only, never on a whole folder by fallback. **Move to folder…** (`MnuMoveToFolder`, `M` on the mosaic) opens the in-app Move dialog (recent destinations first, filter, New folder under the selected row, Browse… system picker as the fallback, which must still land inside a watched folder); a New folder created in that dialog then used as the Move destination is folded into the Move journal (`absorbCreatedFolder`) so **one Undo** returns the files and removes the empty folder. **Move to recent** (`MnuMoveToRecent`) lists the last 8 destinations per project (`DestinationRecents`). Organize apply must not mutate bound `OrganizePreviewItem` off the UI thread (`OrganizeService.MarkPreviewApplied` after await).
- **Folder tree** shows real folders, including empty ones, under local watched sources (`FolderTreeBuilder`, listed off the UI thread; listing a cloud placeholder folder reads metadata only, never hydrates). Counts include sub-folders. Tree sort is per project (`FolderTreeSort_{projectId}`). New folder (toolbar `BtnNewFolder`, tree header `BtnTreeNewFolder`, tree menu, Ctrl+Shift+N) adds an inline name row that is created on Enter / focus loss (Esc cancels); Rename (F2) is inline; Delete is empty folders only with a confirmation; roots can't be renamed or deleted. All go through `FileOpService` and are undoable. Dragging tiles (mouse only) onto a tree folder moves them (`AssetDrag`): outside select mode the tile (or the selection when it is part of it); in select mode only a drag that starts on a selected tile, otherwise it is a range select.
- Organize is on-disk, dry-run first, ask destination each run. Auto-organize is opt-in per source.
- Tag organize asks which parent chain. Assigning a tag applies configured implicits (transitive, cycle-safe).
- Tags page is an Eagle-style board. **All / Uncategorized / Starred are pinned at the top of the left group column** (in that order), then user groups (`TagPanelBuilder.BuildBoard`). Selecting a group stays in that column; child / sub-tags of the selected group are a **wrapping color-dot chip mosaic** in the next column (`RepTagChildren` `WrapLayout` under A–Z headers, `TxtTagChildrenHeader`) — not a tall full-width list. Creating or selecting a tag opens the group that contains it (`TagBoardExpand`). Uncategorized display name stays **Uncategorized**; automation id stays `BtnTagGroup_Ungrouped` (`IsUngrouped` / `AutomationIdOverride`) so the Library assign flyout does not become `BtnTagGroup_Uncategorized`. Search All chips have no `ParentId`. Tags inside a group are **A–Z with letter headers** (`TagAlphaIndex`). The Tags mosaic groups by **selected tag / next child / next child** (`TagMosaicGroups`; Priority then name). Keep `GrdTagAssets` and `TxtTagMosaicGroup_*` headers. **Select mode** on the Tags mosaic uses `TglTagSelectMode` / `TxtTagSelectionCount` (`TagsViewModel.IsSelectMode`, same `SelectMode.Summary` / checkmarks); press-and-hold / click-and-hold on a tile enters select mode and selects that item (`SelectMode.EnterFromHold`) without opening overlay; range drag is `RangeSelect` (press then drag, touch press-and-hold then drag). Bulk actions stay off (Open only, `MnuTagOpen`). Grouped mosaic tiles are tab-stop; Enter opens the focused or clicked tile, not the first asset. Keep `SelTagScope` on the board scroller, `SelTagScopeAll` / `SelTagScopeStarred` / `BtnTagGroup_Ungrouped` on those rows, and `RepTagBoard`. Disk organize stays in the details column. Comma/newline batch-create uses `TagNameList`. Library tag browse (`SelTags` / `TreTagsBrowse`) is a wrapping chip mosaic (`BrowseTags` / `TagBrowseMosaic.Flatten`, `BtnTagChip_*`) — not a same-width TreeView column — and toggles multiple tags with Any / All / None (`TagFilter`). Preview tags are wrap chips with × sized to text (`ChipWrapLayout` on `LstTags` / overlay `LstGalleryOverlayTags` / `LstGalleryWindowTags` — not fixed `VariableSizedWrapGrid` cells); keep `LstTags` / `BtnRemoveTag_*` / `BtnBrowseTags`. Manual/Implied are not face labels — Implied chips use muted opacity (`AssignedTagChrome.Opacity` / `ChromeOpacity`), source (+ optional k/n) lives in tooltip / `ChipAutomationName`; multi-select partial chips still show k/n on the face. `BtnBrowseTags` is the + Add tag flyout. Selecting a tag-board group uses an accent outline (`BindHelpers.SelectedBorder` on `IsExpanded`) — no face "On" label; keep `BtnTagGroup_*` / `BtnTagGroup_Ungrouped`. Chip context: Filter in Library (`ApplySingleTagFilter` + `NavLibrary`), star, rename (focus `TxtRenameTag`), Add/Move to group (root groups via `TagGroups`), remove from this group, delete. Keep `MnuFilterTag` / `MnuRenameTag` / `MnuAddToGroup_*` / `MnuMoveToGroup_*`. Library `SelBrowseMode` / `SelTagMatch` follow `IsTagBrowse` / `TagFilterMode` on construct and Loaded — do not write the Folders/All defaults back. `SelectNode` stamps `SelectedName` and a rename baseline for every path (chip, group, create). `LoadSelectionAsync` applies the catalog name only when the tag changed or the box still matches that baseline — a cleared or edited box on the same tag is kept (`TagSelection.ShouldApplyLoadedName`).
- Library mosaic: viewing any **folder prefix** (source root or nested subfolder) groups tiles by the first 1â€“2 child folders under that prefix. Header text is `Selected / Sub / Sub` (`FolderGroups`) as a **compact caption row** (Fluent `Folder` + `TxtFolderGroup_`), laid out by `MosaicRows` / `JustifiedMosaicLayout` at `GalleryMedia.FolderHeaderHeight` (28 DIP) — not the asset mosaic tile layout and not a 32:1 LinedFlow slot. `MosaicRows` flushes leftover tiles so every header is a full-width caption; missing mid-row headers were that LinedFlow hack. Search, tag browse, and the all-library view stay a flat mosaic. **Sort:** Library `BtnMosaicSort` / Tags `BtnTagMosaicSort` are DropDownButtons in the select-mode cluster (Fluent `ArrowSort` + current field/direction label). `RadioMenuFlyoutItem`s pick field and direction (`SetMosaicSortFieldCommand` / `SetMosaicSortDescendingCommand`). Per-view LocalSettings (`MosaicSort_{projectId}_{Folders|TagBrowse|Tags}` via `MosaicSortOrder`, with legacy `MosaicSort_{projectId}` fallback). Default is **Date taken (newest)** (`COALESCE(DateTaken, DateModified, DateAdded)`); also Date modified / Date added / Name / Size / Type / Rating. Library `Loaded` calls `ReloadMosaicSortAsync` so a Tags sort is applied on return. Sort runs in the catalog `ORDER BY` (`GetAssetsAsync` / prefix / tag filter / FTS) — do not load the whole library to sort in process. Folder headers stay non-assets and keep group-title order; tiles inside a group keep SQL order. **Row height** (`SldRowHeight`, icon + text) lives on the Library **status/bottom bar** with `TxtStatus`, not the search row. **Select mode:** the top-left `TglSelectMode` ToggleButton (Fluent `Multiselect` + "Select", above the breadcrumb in the mosaic column; `LibraryViewModel.IsSelectMode`) turns multi-select on; press-and-hold / click-and-hold on a mosaic tile also enters select mode and selects that tile (`SelectMode.EnterFromHold`) without opening overlay. Off is `ItemsViewSelectionMode.Single` (preview click); on is `Multiple` so a plain click or tap toggles tiles — never Extended Ctrl/Shift. `ItemContainer` draws the checkmark. Space opens overlay instead of toggling. In Select mode, pointer-down on a tile then drag selects the **contiguous mosaic range** from that first item through the last highlighted item (`RangeSelect` / `ApplyMosaicRange`; skip folder headers — not a marquee). Touch: **press-and-hold, then drag**. Overlay pan is not stolen (`AllowsGesture` is false while the overlay is open; mosaic `IsHitTestVisible` stays off). `TxtSelectionCount` shows `N selected` (or a hint when on and empty; `SelectMode.Summary`, refreshed from `RefreshSelectionSummary`). When select mode is on **and** tiles are selected, Library chrome shows **Tag selected…** (`BtnTagSelected`, Fluent `Tag` + text, Accent) which opens the existing assign flyout (`FlyAssignTags` / `BtnBrowseTags`). Hide the CTA when mode is off or the selection is empty (`SelectMode.ShowBatchTagCta` / `ShowTagSelectedCta`). Toggling off keeps the selection. Open / Move / Copy / Delete / Add to room / tag assign use the same `_selection`. Headers are not assets — skip them for selection, gallery, thumbs, and organize. Navigate only on header tap (or Open on a header); do not navigate from mosaic selection, arrow keys, or right-click. Asset context flyout stays on the tab-stop `ItemContainer` so Menu / `ContextRequested` opens Open / Delete / Move / Copy; headers cancel `ContextRequested` (`ShouldShowAssetContextFlyout`) so those commands stay off headers.- Library-first until the matching 0.x slice. Do not invent Rooms canvas, gamedev formats, or AI auto-tag unless that minor is the work (see Version). Cloud is a **bonus**, not a numbered main slice and not the next increment after Library.
